>> title: Meatloaf Cupcakes
>> servings: 12
>> source: https://www.thespruceeats.com/meatloaf-muffins-3058333

Heat the oven to 350F. Lightly spray a #muffin pan{12-cup} with nonstick cooking spray or grease with shortening or melted butter.

In a medium #skillet{}, heat @olive oil{1%tablespoon} over medium heat. Add @onion{0.5}(finely chopped) to the pan and sauté until lightly browned and tender, about ~{3%minutes}.

Add @garlic{1%clove}(minced) and cook, stirring, for ~{1%minute} longer.

In a bowl, combine @ground beef chuck{1.5%pounds} with @ketchup{0.5%cup}, @breadcrumbs{0.5%cup}(soft fine), @egg{1}(beaten), @Worcestershire sauce{1%teaspoon}, @salt{0.75%teaspoon}, @black pepper{0.5%teaspoon}(ground), @oregano{0.5%teaspoon}(dried), and @thyme{0.5%teaspoon}(dried).

Add the sautéed vegetables and mix until blended, being careful not to overmix.

Pack the meat mixture into the prepared muffin cups.

Bake the meatloaf muffins for ~{20%minutes}.

Top each meatloaf muffin with about @ketchup{1%tablespoon} of the remaining ketchup. Return to the oven and bake for about ~{5-10%minutes} longer.

Cook until an instant-read thermometer registers at least 160F when inserted into the center of a muffin.